{% doc %}
  Looks up the user and mints a temporary token scoped to the verification TTL.

  temporary_token takes its lifetime in HOURS, so USER_EMAIL_VERIFICATION_TTL_HOURS
  is passed straight through as expires_in. (An earlier version converted it to
  minutes and passed it as valid_for as well; because the platform resolves the
  lifetime as `valid_for || expires_in`, that produced a token good for 1440
  HOURS - 60 days - rather than the documented 24.)

  The token is not single use - replay is handled in verify.liquid, which
  reports an already confirmed address rather than an error, because mail
  clients and link scanners do follow these URLs more than once.

  @param {string} email - The address to send the link to
  @param {string} host - The host the link should point at
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign ttl_hours = context.constants.USER_EMAIL_VERIFICATION_TTL_HOURS | default: 24 | plus: 0

  function user = 'modules/user/queries/user/find', email: email, id: null, with_token: true, expires_in: ttl_hours

  comment
    Only look for a profile once there is a user to look it up by: queries/profiles/find
    logs an ERROR when every identifier is blank, and an unknown address is a
    normal, unauthenticated request here - not something worth an error line.
  endcomment
  assign profile = null
  if user.id
    function profile = 'modules/user/queries/profiles/find', user_id: user.id, id: null, uuid: null, first_name: null, last_name: null
  endif

  assign object = { "email": email, "host": host, "id": user.id, "token": user.token, "profile": profile, "ttl_hours": ttl_hours }

  return object
%}
